course: dictionary
lesson: 5880
title: Reading the clues: manifesto
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manifesto is a written statement that says what a group believes and what it promises to do. You can work out this meaning from the clues around the word. «A political party is a group with shared ideas that tries to win elections; its manifesto is its list of plans and promises.» The words plans and promises tell you what a manifesto contains.
explain: Look at the words near the word too. «A slogan is a short catchy phrase; the full list of promises is in a party's manifesto, which most people never read.» A slogan is short, but a manifesto is the full list. So a manifesto is longer and fuller than a slogan.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «A political party is like a team built around ideas: people who think alike join together, choose candidates and write a plan of promises called a manifesto.» Put "a plan of promises" in place of "a manifesto" and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A manifesto is a written public statement.
fact: A political party writes a manifesto to say what it believes and what it promises to do if it is elected.
fact: Any artist, group or person can write a manifesto to share bold ideas and aims.
fact: «Manifesto» can also be spelled manifestoes in the plural.
fact: Useful phrases: «election manifesto», «manifesto promise», «write a manifesto».
exercise: «A slogan is a short catchy phrase; the full list of promises is in a party's manifesto, which most people never read.» What is a manifesto? | A short catchy phrase | A card you post in a box | A type of football team | *The full written list of a party's promises
exercise: «A slogan is like the cover of a book: three words you cannot forget, while the real promises sit inside a long document called a manifesto.» Which word tells you a manifesto is long? | cover | *long | three | forget
exercise: Ruby is standing for school council and writes her own manifesto. What is she doing? | Cooking lunch for the class | Winning a race at sports day | Reading a library book | *Telling people what she believes and what she promises to do
test: «A political party is a group with shared ideas that tries to win elections; its manifesto is its list of plans and promises.» What does a party's manifesto contain? | Its shopping list | *Its list of plans and promises | Its team kit | Its favourite songs
test: What does «write a manifesto» mean? | To write a letter to a friend | *To write a public statement of your beliefs and promises | To draw a picture of a team | To copy a book
exam: Which best describes a manifesto? | A kind of race | *A written statement of beliefs and promises, shared in public | A short slogan of three words | A type of cake
